      "answer": {
        "question": "What does a child learn from building blocks?",
        "text": "Building asks a child to picture a shape, choose an order and try again when it falls.[^1] Those are the first steps of planning, and a tower that topples teaches as much as one that stands. Sit nearby, name what you see and let your child decide the next block.[^2]"
